Z||000001||Cheever3000||10-10-2001||06:28 PM||||I don't care what anybody else says, the Atkins diet is the only thing that EVER worked for me, and it works like a miracle.  Okay, sure, I'm currently overweight, but I'm just enjoying the carbs at this point in my life.  Plus my spouse won't go on it with me, and that would help.<P>You don't need to buy anything to do the Atkins low-carb thing, just look up his books in the library.<P>There are so many people who think it's a "fad" diet or whatever, that if I come back to this thread to read replies like that I'll just get angry, so this will be all I am going to say about it.  It works for me.  <BR>||||reg||6
Z||000002||WampusCat||10-10-2001||06:38 PM||||Lift weights.  Muscle tissue burns lotsa calories.  I don't do any complicated workout, just dead lifts, pull-ups, 1 arm press, about 15-20 min/3-5 days/week.  Do some aerobic stuff too.  Run, walk, bike, Kung Fu, whatever.  Take it easy on the cheese, sugar, corn, taters, white rice, white bread.  Eat plenty of lean protein.  Check out "the zone" from the library(or sugarbusters, adkins whatever, all similar message.) Beer is fattening, I still drink plenty but if I wanted to lose a few lbs fast, I'd consider cutting it out for a few weeks.  I'm kinda scared of supplements other than multi-vitamins.  Caffiene helps keep the metabalism stoked, maybe some green tea a couple times during the day in addition to morning coffee is that doesn't make you too jumpy.||||reg||1
Z||000003||hugh||10-10-2001||06:55 PM||||I've told lots of people about the Atkins diet.They've lost weight and their cholesterol has also gone down.The only problem I have with it is it's boring.You will never be hungry on this diet!If you're hungry,just eat a dozen chicken wings with a Coors light or diet soda(Aspertame is no good for you).||||reg||14
