Z||000011||Formula88||10-10-2001||09:58 PM||||On the advise of my doctor, when I was in my 20's, I went to the Diet Center.  I lost 97 pounds in under 6 months and maintained low blood pressure and excellent health.  I've since gained weight back, but that's cuz I don't do what I know I'm supposed to do.  It's real simple.  <P>Eat lean protein and fresh fruit and vegetables.  Take supplements to make sure you're getting everything your body needs.  Get some aerobic exercise (walking is usually best when starting out).  As you get in shape, strength training can give even better results, as muscle tissue burns more calories than fat tissue, even at rest.<P>No real miracles, here.  Cut out the carbs, unless you're a body builder, you'll get all you need anyway.  Don't forget the fresh fruit and veggies.<P>Oh, and the juice of 1 lemon every day.  That helps keep the skin resiliant.  I had no problems with loose skin or stretch marks after loosing 97 pounds on this diet.  ||||reg||1
