Z||000013||Mach10||10-10-2001||10:34 PM||||Try taking up swimming. About 2km per day will shave off more weight than you thought you could ever lose. After the first month, 2km is NOTHING.*<P>All I can say is excercise. Cardio is the best way. I'm not going to slag "fad diets" because for all I know, they might work. I'm more of a traditionalist. Your genetics determines your weight. But it does this by factoring in your lifestyle. Burning 5000 cals per day swimming alone will keep your "balance" weight at a much more pleasant level...<P>Oh, Good luck! It won't be easy, but it'll be worth it!<P>*I did competitive swimming for 5 years. Trust me.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||10
